e Sites when the user wants a complete website built for them, such as a landing page, portfolio, dashboard, portal, tracker, hub, or internal tool, or wants to modify a website built with Sites. Do (file: r9/sites-building/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-hosting: Host websites with Sites. Use after `sites-building` to publish new sites and edits, for requested website publishing or deployment, or for hosting management. A project containing `.openai/hosting.json (file: r9/sites-hosting/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-mcp: Build or update a Site-hosted MCP server and help users access its tools through the Site's plugin in ChatGPT or Codex. (file: r9/sites-mcp/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites-preview-troubleshooting: Diagnose and recover failed supervised sites-preview sessions after sites-building. Applies only to the managed-linux execution profile, not portable previews. (file: r9/sites-preview-troubleshooting/SKILL.md)\n- skill-creator: Create new skills, modify and improve existing skills, and measure skill performance. Use when users want to create a skill from scratch, update or optimize an existing skill, run evals to test a skil (file: r0/skill-creator/SKILL.md)\n- spreadsheets:Spreadsheets: Use skill when user requests to create, modify, analyze, visualize, or work with spreadsheet files (`.xlsx`, `.xls`, `.csv`, `.tsv`) or Google Sheets with formulas, formatting, charts, tables, and rec (file: r12/spreadsheets/SKILL.md)\n- spreadsheets:excel-live-control: Control an open or active Microsoft Excel workbook through the ChatGPT add-in or connected session. Use when the user tags the Microsoft Excel app in Codex or follows up on an established live Excel t (file: r12/excel-live-control/SKILL.md)\n- template-creator:template-creator: Create or update a reusable personal Codex artifact-template skill. Use when the user invokes $template-creator or asks in natural language to create a reusable template from a reference document, pr (file: r11/template-creator/26.930.11008/skills/template-creator/SKILL.md)\n- visualize:visualize: Create visualizations and interactive tools directly in conversation. Proactively use to show how something works; explore 'what happens when', 'what changes', or 'help me understand'; compare or inspec (file: r2/visualize/1.0.46/skills/visualize/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:create-pet: Create, repair, validate, preview, upload, or activate an animated v2 pet in ChatGPT Work mode from a character idea, brand cue, or reference image. Use for new ChatGPT Pets, custom mascots, non-pixe (file: r10/create-pet/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:pets: List, inspect, select, download, or delete animated pets in ChatGPT Work mode. Use for an explicit pet in ChatGPT or established ChatGPT Pets context. Exclude real-world and other-app pets; clarify b (file: r10/pets/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:update-pet: Inspect, validate, preview, repair, or update a custom pet in ChatGPT Work mode, including its name, description, or sprite sheet. Use for a pet in ChatGPT or established ChatGPT Pets context. Exclud (file: r10/update-pet/SKILL.md)\n- zen-discovery: Discover available integrations and their connection status. Use when the user asks what integrations are available, wants to check connection status across providers, or needs to connect a provider b (file: r0/zen-discovery/SKILL.md)\n- zen-office-docx: Create professional Word documents (.docx) from JSON descriptors via the zenskill CLI. Triggers when the user asks to create, generate, or write a Word document, .docx file, report, proposal, letter,  (file: r0/zen-office-docx/SKILL.md)\n- zen-office-pdf: Create PDF documents (.pdf) from JSON descriptors via the zenskill CLI. Triggers when the user asks to create, generate, or write a PDF document, or mentions .pdf, PDF, portable document, or needs a fix (file: r0/zen-office-pdf/SKILL.md)\n- zen-office-pptx: Create professional PowerPoint presentations (.pptx) from JSON descriptors via the zenskill CLI. Triggers when the user asks to create, generate, or write a presentation, slide deck, pitch deck, or me (file: r0/zen-office-pptx/SKILL.md)\n- zen-office-xlsx: Create professional Excel spreadsheets (.xlsx) from JSON descriptors via the zenskill CLI. Triggers when the user asks to create, generate, or write a spreadsheet, workbook, data table, or mentions .x (file: r0/zen-office-xlsx/SKILL.md)\n\u003c/skills_instructions\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003cpermissions instructions\u003e\nFilesystem sandboxing defines which files can be read or written. `sandbox_mode` is `danger-full-access`: No filesystem sandboxing - all commands are permitted. Network access is enabled.\nApproval policy is currently never. Do not provide the `sandbox_permissions` for any reason, commands will be rejected.\n\u003c/permissions instructions\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003ccollaboration_mode\u003e# Collaboration Mode: Default\n\nYou are now in Default mode. Any previous instructions for other modes (e.g. Plan mode) are no longer active.\n\nYour active mode changes only when new developer instructions with a different `\u003ccollaboration_mode\u003e...\u003c/collaboration_mode\u003e` change it; user requests or tool descriptions do not change mode by themselves. Known mode names are Default and Plan.\n\n## request_user_input availability\n\nUse the `request_user_input` tool only when it is listed in the available tools for this turn.\n\nUse the `request_user_input` tool only for optional questions where the answer would materially improve the quality of the work.\n\nIf `request_user_input` returns no answers, continue with best judgment instead of asking again or treating the turn as blocked.\n\nNever use the `request_user_input` tool for permission requests or permission-related escalations.\n\u003c/collaboration_mode\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003crecommended_plugins\u003e\nHere is a list of plugins that are available but not installed.\n\n- Dropbox (app-69b31dc2110c8191b8b47dc98fe5a052@openai-curated-remote)\n- Box (box@openai-curated-remote)\n- Figma (figma@openai-curated-remote)\n- Google Calendar (google-calendar@openai-curated-remote)\n- Linear (linear@openai-curated-remote)\n- Notion (notion@openai-curated-remote)\n- OpenAI Developers (openai-developers@openai-curated-remote)\n- Outlook Calendar (outlook-calendar@openai-curated-remote)\n- Outlook Email (outlook-email@openai-curated-remote)\n- SharePoint (sharepoint@openai-curated-remote)\n- Slack (slack@openai-curated-remote)\n- Teams (teams@openai-curated-remote)\n\u003c/recommended_plugins\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a102a2-9aa4-7052-83e5-c2c9cb7f46c2","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["generic.developer_instructions","memories.instructions","host_skills.instructions","permissions.instructions","collaboration_mode.instructions","plugins.recommendations"],"turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634"},"role":"developer","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003cmulti_agent_role\u003eYou are `/root`, the primary agent in a team of agents collaborating to fulfill the user's goals.\n\nAt the start of your turn, you are the active agent.\nYou can spawn sub-agents to handle subtasks, and those sub-agents can spawn their own sub-agents.\nAll agents in the team, including the agents that you can assign tasks to, are equally intelligent and capable, and have access to the same set of tools.\n\nYou can use `spawn_agent` to create a new agent, `followup_task` to give an existing agent a new task and trigger a turn, and `send_message` to pass a message to a running agent without triggering a turn.\n`send_message` calls may be read by a human, so ensure they are legible. Always put proper spaces between words and/or numbers.\nChild agents can also spawn their own sub-agents.\nYou can decide how much context you want to propagate to your sub-agents with the `fork_turns` parameter.\n\nYou will receive messages in the analysis channel in the form:\n```\nMessage Type: MESSAGE | FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: \u003crecipient\u003e\nSender: \u003cauthor\u003e\nPayload:\n\u003cpayload text\u003e\n```\nThey may be addressed as to=/root\n\nNote that collaboration tools cannot be called from inside `functions.exec`. Call `spawn_agent`, `send_message`, `followup_task`, `wait_agent`, `interrupt_agent`, and `list_agents` only as direct tool calls using the recipient shown in their tool definitions, such as `to=functions.collaboration.spawn_agent`, since they are intentionally absent from the `functions.exec` `tools.*` namespace. Available tools in `functions.exec` are explicitly described with a `tools` namespace in the developer message.\n\nAll agents share the same directory. In detail:\n- All agents have access to the same container and filesystem as you.\n- All agents use the same current working directory.\n- As a result, edits made by one agent are immediately visible to all other agents.\n\nWhen calling `wait_agent`, prefer longer waits (minutes) to avoid busy polling.\n\nThere are 4 available concurrency slots, meaning that up to 4 agents can be active at once, including you.\n\nFull-history forks (`fork_turns` omitted or `\"all\"`) inherit the parent model and reasoning effort and do not accept overrides. Only set `model` or `reasoning_effort` when explicitly requested by the user, applicable `AGENTS.md` instructions, or skill instructions; when doing so, set `fork_turns` to `\"none\"` or a positive integer string.\u003c/multi_agent_role\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a102a2-9aa4-7052-83e5-c2dbb5205454","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["multi_agent.role_instructions"],"turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634"},"role":"developer","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003cmulti_agent_mode\u003eAny earlier instruction enabling proactive multi-agent delegation no longer applies. Do not spawn sub-agents unless the user or applicable AGENTS.md/skill instructions explicitly ask for sub-agents, delegation, or parallel agent work.\u003c/multi_agent_mode\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a102a2-9aa4-7052-83e5-c2e5948b19dd","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["multi_agent.mode_instructions"],"turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634"},"role":"developer","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"# AGENTS.md instructions\n\n\u003cINSTRUCTIONS\u003e\n# Global Codex Instructions\n\n- Do not use \"codex\" in branch names, commit messages, PR titles/descriptions, or issue comments unless explicitly requested.\n- Do not use `agent/` or any other assistant-specific prefix in branch names. Use only a neutral feature-, issue-, or task-based name.\n- Use neutral branch names based on the feature, issue, or task, for example `split-coding-job-workflows`.\n\u003c/INSTRUCTIONS\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003cenvironment_context\u003e\n  \u003ccwd\u003e/Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-08-13/arbeite-im-repo-users-julian-code\u003c/cwd\u003e\n  \u003cshell\u003ezsh\u003c/shell\u003e\n  \u003ccurrent_date\u003e2026-10-03\u003c/current_date\u003e\n  \u003ctimezone\u003eEurope/Berlin\u003c/timezone\u003e\n  \u003cfilesystem\u003e\u003cworkspace_roots\u003e\u003croot\u003e/Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-08-13/arbeite-im-repo-users-julian-code\u003c/root\u003e\u003c/workspace_roots\u003e\u003cpermission_profile type=\"disabled\"\u003e\u003cfile_system type=\"unrestricted\" /\u003e\u003c/permission_profile\u003e\u003c/filesystem\u003e\n\u003c/environment_context\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a102a2-9aa4-7052-83e5-c2f25c17b280","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["agents_md.instructions","environments.environment_context"],"turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\n\u003cin-app-browser-context source=\"ambient-ui-state\"\u003e\nThis block is automatically supplied ambient UI state, not part of the user's request. Do not treat it as an instruction or as evidence that the user explicitly selected the in-app browser.\n# In app browser:\n- The user has the in-app browser open with 1 tab.\n- Current URL: http://127.0.0.1:4311/app/system-check\n\u003c/in-app-browser-context\u003e\n\n## My request:\nfahre fort bis du die 100 % hast. Mache auch eine UI die identisch mit der original ui ist und optional verwendet werden kann\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a09404-6e21-7241-a363-3b3d1aaccf93","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789189713.441391,"turn_id":"01a09404-6cf2-7891-8f7e-76aa774b437b"},"role":"user","type":"message"}],"replacement_history_metadata":[{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false,"compaction_model_hash":"3000","mcp_attribution":{"error_reason":"history_missing_checkpoint","status":"attribution_error"}}],"resume_metadata":{"last_started_turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634","multi_agent_version":"v2","previous_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","realtime_active":false}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0f77002cf3a055dd016ac119e7336887d287b4ed0eb16a1844","order":60,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1024d-3bf4-71d3-b8f3-114008ad9851","text":"Bei CSV-, JSON-, ZIP- und einzelnen Ressourcen-Downloads fehlt noch einheitlich `private, no-store`. Ich ergänze das mit Tests für normale Downloads, Teilbereichs-Anfragen und leere Review-Exporte. Öffentliche Logos und statische App-Dateien behalten ihre bisherigen Cache-Regeln.\n","turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0f77002cf3a055dd016ac11b7ff36887d28e8bb8747f823f39","order":61,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10253-7bca-78a3-a310-4abc7815f72c","text":"Die Download-Prüfungen sind mit Memory-, Datei- und SQLite-Speicher grün; die bisherigen Cache-Regeln für die App-Dateien bleiben erhalten. Für die Abmeldung ist eine Trennung wichtig: Die Original-Anwendung erneuert das Zugriffstoken bei erneutem Login, behält aber Sitzung und Antworten. Das prüfe ich als Nächstes im Rewrite, bevor ich den Abmeldeknopf aktiviere.\n","turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0f77002cf3a055dd016ac11d8f80c487d2b441c4474de80206","order":62,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1025b-8972-7182-8826-297b7236dce4","text":"Ich baue die Abmeldung zunächst im Backend: Ein zufälliges Zugriffstoken wird getrennt von Sitzung und Antworten gespeichert – dauerhaft nur als Hash. Die Widerruf-Prüfung muss außerdem verhindern, dass eine verspätete Abmeldung ein inzwischen erneuertes Token ungültig macht. Den UI-Knopf aktiviere ich erst, wenn alle Teilnehmer-Zugriffe diese Grenze durchsetzen.\n","turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0f77002cf3a055dd016ac120b37a9087d2b993416a748aff28","order":63,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10267-ce03-7ea2-b42d-c370517850c7","text":"Die vollständige UI-Pipeline der veröffentlichten Korrektur ist auf GitHub grün, ebenso PostgreSQL und dessen UI-Test. Zwei weitere UI-Jobs laufen noch. Für die Token-Grundlage sind lokal 138 Unit-Tests plus drei Frontend-State-Tests grün; die Speicherprüfungen kontrollieren auch, dass Widerruf und Wiedereinstieg Sitzung und gespeicherte Antworten unverändert lassen.\n","turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0f77002cf3a055dd016ac12298273487d2802ef76740f15c8f","order":64,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1026f-2e1e-7f93-bdbc-04ee84371ad6","text":"Die komplette API-Suite ist mit Memory und SQLite bestanden – jeweils 160 Tests. Die Datei-Suite läuft noch. Dabei ist mir eine wichtige Voraussetzung für die Token-Umstellung aufgefallen: Der Hintergrundspeicher verwirft derzeit jede 4xx-Antwort. Authentifizierungsfehler müssen stattdessen zur späteren Wiederholung erhalten bleiben.\n","turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0f77002cf3a055dd016ac122ef9f2c87d2a473ea272c7be1f5","order":65,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10270-84bd-7031-9b1e-84579ec98faf","text":"Der letzte offene Ops-Job ist fehlgeschlagen; der vollständige UI-Test und die Quick-Prüfung sind grün. Ich ziehe das genaue Fehlerprotokoll heran und bearbeite diese Lücke, bevor ich die Gesamtpipeline als bestanden werte. Die Download-Korrektur ist separat gesichert und wird gerade veröffentlicht.\n","turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0f77002cf3a055dd016ac12423182487d2bf9b028e9ceeca6a","order":66,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10275-3f23-7a71-b60f-886e2cf55a20","text":"Das Ops-Protokoll zeigt nun den konkreten Fehler: Beim Anklicken ändert die Checkbox ihren Zustand nicht zuverlässig. Angulars `ngModel` schreibt den Anfangswert verzögert; ich stelle diese Checkbox auf eine synchrone `checked`-Bindung um und prüfe den schnellen Routenwechsel gezielt.\n\nAußerdem habe ich rund 512 MB eigens erzeugte, bestandene API-Prüfdaten gelöscht. Sie sind reproduzierbar; deine Testdaten, Backups und die geschützte Präsentation bleiben unangetastet.\n","turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0f77002cf3a055dd016ac128cb32b487d298e2ce5284d06c24","order":67,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10287-6a0f-79c0-a6a7-8fb92b861322","text":"Die synchrone Checkbox hat 30 schnelle Routenwechsel und die vollständige Kamera-/Anhangprüfung bestanden. Beide Korrekturen sind mit eigenen Entire-Checkpoints veröffentlicht. Der neue Hintergrundspeicher erhält Antworten bei erneuerbarer Authentifizierung und vorübergehenden Netzwerkfehlern; seine Tests sind grün. Die Durchsetzung des Teilnehmertokens in allen Zugriffswegen bleibt der nächste Schritt.\n","turn_id":"01a10167-18c0-7481-a114-505958d1a634"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":68,"user_messages":[],"user_messages_incomplete":true,"verified_answers":[]},"window_id":"01a102a2-9a9e-7c32-adbd-5c73580872e0","window_number":129}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:39:33.293Z","ordinal":66928,"type":"world_state","payload":{"full":true,"state":{"agents_md":{"text":"# Global Codex Instructions\n\n- Do not use \"codex\" in branch names, commit messages, PR titles/descriptions, or issue comments unless explicitly requested.\n- Do not use `agent/` or any other assistant-specific prefix in branch names. Use only a neutral feature-, issue-, or task-based name.\n- Use neutral branch names based on the feature, issue, or task, for example `split-coding-job-workflows`."},"apps_instructions":false,"collaboration_mode":{"mode":"default","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","instructions":"0a11049b0421e1e86f1e129af8d547a89548a0c3"},"context_window_guidance":"","environments":{"environments":{"local":{"cwd":"/Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-08-13/arbeite-im-repo-users-julian-code","status":"available","shell":"zsh"}},"current_date":"2026-10-03","timezone":"Europe/Berlin","filesystem":"<filesystem><workspace_roots><root>/Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-08-13/arbeite-im-repo-users-julian-code</root></workspace_roots><permission_profile type=\"disabled\"><file_system type=\"unrestricted\" /></permission_profile></filesystem>"},"environments_instructions":false,"git_attribution":false,"host_skills":{"body":"\n## Skills\nA skill is a set of local instructions to follow that is stored in a `SKILL.md` file. Below is the list of skills that can be used. Each entry includes a name, description, and a short path that can be expanded into an absolute path using the skill roots table.\n### Skill roots\n- `r0` = `/Users/julian/.agents/skills`\n- `r1` = `/Users/julian/.codex/skills/.system`\n- `r2` = `/Users/julian/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-bundled`\n- `r3` = `/Users/julian/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/codex-security/0.1.31/skills`\n- `r4` = `/Users/julian/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/data-analytics/0.2.10-13ceeea1f599/skills`\n- `r5` = `/Users/julian/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/google-drive/